Ladybird stops a fetch’s network request when the fetch is aborted or
terminated, not only when an element stops it, so an aborted request’s
callbacks stop rooting the fetch’s realm. Blink does the same:
FetchManager::Loader::Abort() cancels the loader’s ThreadableLoader, and
XMLHttpRequest::InternalAbort() cancels the XHR’s loader. So does
WebKit, where FetchLoader::stop() and XMLHttpRequest::abort() cancel
their loaders. And Gecko’s FetchDriver::RunAbortAlgorithm() and
XMLHttpRequestMainThread::CloseRequest() cancel the channel, with
NS_BINDING_ABORTED as the reason.
